1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,401
Welcome to Prism AI, a Windows workspace for research and writing.

2
00:00:05,401 --> 00:00:10,312
This narrated tour follows the supplied version 7.1 interface screenshots.

3
00:00:10,312 --> 00:00:16,204
The latest published release may look different, so check the release notes

4
00:00:16,204 --> 00:00:17,677
for current features.

5
00:00:18,477 --> 00:00:23,327
Prism has two desktop apps. Prism Chat brings projects, conversations,

6
00:00:23,327 --> 00:00:29,148
research, and notes together. Prism Studio is for writing and revising LaTeX

7
00:00:29,148 --> 00:00:33,998
papers and presentations. Start in Chat to explore an idea,

8
00:00:33,998 --> 00:00:39,818
then move your outline into Studio when you are ready to write.

9
00:00:40,618 --> 00:00:45,621
Projects give related conversations and research a shared home. The sample project

10
00:00:45,621 --> 00:00:50,624
shown here is clearly labeled as fictional and separate from your work.

11
00:00:50,624 --> 00:00:55,626
It is a safe way to explore the interface. Check the preview

12
00:00:55,626 --> 00:01:00,629
and release notes before relying on any feature in your installed version.

13
00:01:01,429 --> 00:01:07,443
In Prism Chat, choose a mode for the task. Ask is for

14
00:01:07,443 --> 00:01:12,955
ordinary conversation. Research can search supported sources and show retrieved material.

15
00:01:12,955 --> 00:01:18,968
Documents is for questions about files you provide. Create helps draft content.

16
00:01:18,968 --> 00:01:24,982
Review responses and sources carefully. A citation or matching quote is not

17
00:01:24,982 --> 00:01:28,489
proof that a larger claim is correct.

18
00:01:29,289 --> 00:01:34,854
The Library brings project evidence and writing materials into one place.

19
00:01:34,854 --> 00:01:40,925
Review retrieved extracts and abstracts, follow citation markers back to source cards,

20
00:01:40,925 --> 00:01:45,984
and organize drafts and documents. The available research sources vary,

21
00:01:45,984 --> 00:01:51,043
and the retrieved material may not include a complete paper.

22
00:01:51,043 --> 00:01:54,585
Verify important claims with the original source.

23
00:01:55,385 --> 00:02:00,562
My Prism and Teach Prism provide ways to shape preferences and guidance.

24
00:02:00,562 --> 00:02:05,739
For example, the writing-style screen analyzes a sample and lets you review

25
00:02:05,739 --> 00:02:10,917
a suggestion before saving it. Teaching items can have their own scope

26
00:02:10,917 --> 00:02:16,094
and priority. Read each screen carefully and approve only the changes you

27
00:02:16,094 --> 00:02:16,526
want.

28
00:02:17,326 --> 00:02:23,277
Prism Studio is the LaTeX writing workspace. Draft papers or presentations,

29
00:02:23,277 --> 00:02:29,770
review proposed edits before applying them, work with references, and compile a

30
00:02:29,770 --> 00:02:35,180
PDF using Tectonic. AI suggestions and references can be wrong,

31
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:41,673
so review changes and verify citations. PDF compilation also depends on a

32
00:02:41,673 --> 00:02:43,296
working TeX setup.

33
00:02:44,096 --> 00:02:49,393
You can configure a local model through Ollama or connect a supported

34
00:02:49,393 --> 00:02:54,248
cloud provider. With a local model, inference runs on your computer,

35
00:02:54,248 --> 00:02:59,104
though downloads and some research features may still need the internet.

36
00:02:59,104 --> 00:03:03,959
Cloud prompts containing your content go to the provider you configure.

37
00:03:03,959 --> 00:03:07,932
Review the provider terms, and never share API keys.

38
00:03:08,732 --> 00:03:14,540
To get started, download the Windows installer from the latest Prism AI

39
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:20,349
release, not the source-code archive. Follow the installation guide, configure a local

40
00:03:20,349 --> 00:03:26,157
model or cloud provider if you want live AI, and begin with

41
00:03:26,157 --> 00:03:31,966
a project. This tour uses supplied version 7.1 screenshots and is illustrative.

42
00:03:31,966 --> 00:03:37,774
The published release is version 3.1.0, so screens and features may differ.

43
00:03:37,774 --> 00:03:42,131
Check the changelog and documentation for the current release.
